usage: freeze_current_comparison.py [-h] --runtime RUNTIME --sources SOURCES
                                    --qualification QUALIFICATION --output
                                    OUTPUT --enclosure ENCLOSURE
                                    --expected-manifest-sha256
                                    EXPECTED_MANIFEST_SHA256 --sources-sha256
                                    SOURCES_SHA256 --qualification-sha256
                                    QUALIFICATION_SHA256
                                    --expected-administration-head
                                    EXPECTED_ADMINISTRATION_HEAD
                                    --enclosure-sha256 ENCLOSURE_SHA256

Freeze 1–4 explicitly exposed local families before any comparison arm runs.
Mac/selected7 only. All six arms use 420 routing / 450 method / 600 complete
wall+CPU seconds and 120 export seconds. This performs one bounded tools
query, never Native routing, a board preflight, source scripts, downloads or
publication. Explicit rights are caller declarations, not legal clearance or
independent/untouched pedigree. Keep administration HEAD and all inputs fixed
while running each protocol with scripts/enclose_current_comparison.py. Record
complete external costs/failures; setup costs are additional. Four GiB startup
headroom is not a future job quota. A failure retains its partial new
namespace; never delete/reuse it automatically.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --runtime RUNTIME
  --sources SOURCES
  --qualification QUALIFICATION
  --output OUTPUT
  --enclosure ENCLOSURE
  --expected-manifest-sha256 EXPECTED_MANIFEST_SHA256
  --sources-sha256 SOURCES_SHA256
  --qualification-sha256 QUALIFICATION_SHA256
  --expected-administration-head EXPECTED_ADMINISTRATION_HEAD
  --enclosure-sha256 ENCLOSURE_SHA256
